## ⚙️ How to Run

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/digital-lost-and-found.git
```

### 2. Open the Project

Open the project folder in **VS Code** or your preferred IDE.

### 3. Run the Frontend

Open `index.html` using a browser or **Live Server** extension in VS Code.

### 4. Start the Backend

If the Spring Boot backend is included:

```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```

Make sure the database configuration is correctly set before starting the application.

---

## 🔄 System Workflow

```text
User
  │
  ▼
Register / Login
  │
  ▼
Authentication
  │
  ├───────────────┐
  ▼               ▼
Report Lost    Report Found
  │               │
  └───────┬───────┘
          ▼
     Database
          │
          ▼
    Search & Match
          │
          ▼
   Private Messaging
          │
          ▼
    Item Recovery
```

---

## 🔒 Security

The system focuses on protecting user information and improving trust during the recovery process.

Key security features include:

* JWT-based authentication
* Authenticated user actions
* Private communication
* Controlled access to user information
* Secure handling of lost/found claims

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The main objectives of the project are:

1. Provide a centralized platform for lost and found items.
2. Make reporting lost or found belongings simple.
3. Help users quickly search for matching items.
4. Protect users' personal information.
5. Enable secure communication between users.
6. Improve the chances of successfully recovering lost belongings.

---

## 🌟 Future Enhancements

The system can be further improved by adding:

* 🤖 AI-powered image matching
* 📍 Location-based item matching
